course: dictionary
lesson: 9431
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word staff is one of them. To know which meaning is right, read the words around it: this is its context. «If you are lost in the museum, ask a member of staff.» The clue is lost in a museum, so staff must mean the people who work there.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «The old shepherd leaned on his staff as he walked up the hill.» Can you lean on people? No, so staff must mean a long, strong stick, and that makes sense.
explain: In music, staff means the five lines that notes are written on. A music lesson is the clue here, so a note on the staff is a note written on those five lines.
fact: Staff means the people who work for a school, shop, hospital or company.
fact: A staff is a long, strong stick used for walking, or carried as a sign of power.
fact: In music, the staff (or stave) is the set of five lines that notes are written on.
fact: «Short-staffed» means there are not enough people to do the work, because some have left or are off sick.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The staff gave us a map of the museum.» What does staff mean here? | A long, strong stick | The five lines used for music | A group of pupils on a trip | *The people who work there
exercise: «The old shepherd leaned on his staff as he walked up the hill.» What is a staff in this sentence? | A room where teachers rest | The five lines of music | *A long, strong stick | A bag of sheep
exercise: «The shop was short-staffed, so we had to wait a long time.» What does short-staffed suggest? | Everyone in the shop was on holiday | The shop was very small | *There were not enough people to do the work | The shop had too much food
test: If you are lost or hurt in a shop, what is the safe thing to do? | Run out of the door | Hide behind the shelves | Wait outside alone | *Ask a member of staff
test: In music, what are the five lines of the staff used for? | *Writing notes on | Walking up hills | Holding up a tent | Showing where the exit is
exam: In which sentence does staff mean a long, strong stick? | «The staff room was quiet at lunchtime.» | *«The wizard raised his staff and the room glowed.» | «The school staff were all at the meeting.» | «Ask a member of staff for help.»
